  "summary": "Root cause: the previous composition test expected the nonblocking fast path to fire on a warmed V probe while the translation FSM was IDLE. rv_iommu_tl_wrap.sv:303-306 shows n_window = (state_q==PT && e3_ptw_active && en_1S_q && !en_2S_q && !ddt_imp_trans_q && !pdt_imp_trans_q && !req_data.is_debug && trans_req_data_i.bank != req_data.bank && !ats_ddtc_valid_i && !debug_req_valid_i && !ats_trans_req_valid_i). A fast hit therefore requires a bank-different cold A walk to be held in PT with the PTW active; an idle hot hit can never be fast. Fix (test-only, no RTL/parameter/assertion changes): (1) case_mode_gating now warms V, then holds a cold A page; N/PN must fast-fire V before A is released, S/P must neither accept nor fast-fire for 60 hold cycles and only then, after A drains, run the same V probe down the normal path; every mode consumes the correct bank/spaddr responses and reaches quiet. (2) case_pn_allocation_with_concurrent_v_probe keeps 2 protected V entries and 15 A fills, adds non-vacuous per-DID fill-count checks, and replaces the invalid idle 'fast hit' survival probe with normal idle hot probes that must complete with zero PTW AR. (3) case_policy_quiet section (c) now performs a real cold-A-hold + V-fast backpressure check: quiet must stay low while A is busy and the fast response is stalled, then the fast response is drained, A is released, and quiet is awaited. (4) case_idle_clear_rewarm proves pre-clear hit / post-clear miss+re-warm / post-rewarm hit purely with idle normal probes and PTW observation (no idle fast requirement), and only clears after quiet. New short helpers hot_probe_no_ptw, count_fills, drain_quiet, fast_prove_under_cold_a, block_then_normal_under_cold_a keep the cases reviewable. Leftover latched_req_fire is explicitly cleared before fresh probes rather than being relied on.",
