  "coverage": [
    "case_mode_gating (S/N/P/PN): now warm V -> hold cold A page 0. N/PN use fast_prove_under_cold_a which asserts req_fire_fast BEFORE release_a, then consumes the V fast response (bank 0 @ 0x80000000) and the A response (bank 1 @ 0x90000000) and drains to quiet. S/P use block_then_normal_under_cold_a: 60 hold cycles with neither accept nor fast (nonblock_fire_o is gated by enable_i, line 316), then release A (bank 1 @ 0x90000000), then the same V probe is accepted and completes via the normal path (bank 0 @ 0x80000000) and drains to quiet. saw_nonblock_fire is asserted set for N/PN and never-set for S/P.",
    "case_pn_allocation_with_concurrent_v_probe: unchanged concurrent-V fast check while cold A page 0 is held (window open, bank differs); keeps the 2 protected V fills and the 1+14=15 A fills; adds non-vacuous per-DID fill counts (count_fills(10) >= 2, count_fills(11) >= 15) and a non-empty guard inside check_all_fills. The former idle 'fast hit' survival probe (invalid because n_window requires PT+PTW active) is replaced by normal idle hot probes for both protected V entries that must complete with NO PTW refill (saw_ptw == false), proving capacity survival without requiring idle fast.",
    "case_policy_quiet (c): now a real cold-A page-1 hold + V-page-0 fast probe with trans_resp_ready_i=0. Asserts fast fire, nonblock_busy_o high, and quiet==false while A is busy and the fast response is backpressured (100 cycles). Then drains the fast V response (ready_i=1), releases A (bank 1 @ 0x90001000), and waits for quiet.",
    "case_idle_clear_rewarm: pre-clear proven by an idle normal hot probe with zero PTW refill; clear applied only after quiet; post-clear proven by an observable PTW refill (saw_ptw) re-arming the same leaf; post-rewarm proven by another idle hot probe with zero PTW refill; ends with drain_quiet. No idle fast requirement remains anywhere.",
    "New helpers: hot_probe_no_ptw, count_fills, drain_quiet, fast_prove_under_cold_a, block_then_normal_under_cold_a. latched_req_fire is explicitly cleared before each fresh probe instead of being consumed as stale state; it is still used legitimately for the V accept that can occur inside release_a()."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Not executed. The exact PTW.AR/response cycle timing (e.g. whether the V fast accept and the A spill drain land in the same cycle) is inferred from tests/nonblock_tl_test.cpp (case_fast_hit_nonblock_on / case_response_backpressure); the parent must run the test to confirm.",
    "Requires that nonblock_busy_o (n_busy) is high on the same pre-edge sample as the fast accept, as assumed by nonblock_tl_test.cpp case_response_backpressure; the added CHECK_AT(req_busy_s, ...) in case_policy_quiet relies on this.",
    "The fill-count assertions use >= (2 for DID10, 15 for DID11) rather than == because the supplied files do not include rv_iommu_iotlb, so it is not verifiable here whether research_o.update also pulses on touch lookups (TouchEnable=1). If research_update_o is replacement-only, exact == 2 / == 15 would also hold; >= keeps the check non-vacuous per DID without risking a spurious failure. Parent can tighten to == after confirming RTL.",
    "No production RTL, test-only composition top (composition_tl_top.sv), or existing legitimate assertions were modified; all changes are confined to tests/composition_tl_test.cpp.",
    "The mode cases now hold A page 0; case_policy_quiet and case_pn rely on distinct A pages (0x20001000 / 0x20000000..0x2000E000) and on the protected V ways (policy_partition_i=1, policy_did_i=10) preventing A fills from evicting V (rv_iommu_tl_wrap.sv:669-672)."
  ]
